/rss/articles/CBMiqAFBVV95cUxPNV9hR2x3QUt5TTQ5Zkttd21IMmoyY0p0QVFPOVR0bVBKRUxmYlYzU2dYWkxJejFxRVlYSlBXR0FqcGZWNVBCNHJ3enpzck1HMWdlWEcwbWtXSUNlSzFFNy1XRnFxM1pscnVDUFQwZXN1OXVXSHZ4eG9fengtQ2c4X2FhbVlkVGp1VFI2S2FZUkFCWWtrOUtUZ1kzZTlia0RkWW55RHBHT1A?oc=5"}, {"title": "The 2nd Congressional District: As Goodlander seeks reelection, three say she hasn’t earned it", "source": "New Hampshire Bulletin", "published": "2026-09-07T07:00:00+00:00", "url": "https://news.google.?oc=5"}], "model": {"prior_margin": 13.59, "prior_sd": 5.11, "poll_margin": 19.44, "poll_sd": 6.68, "poll_weight": 0.37, "fundamentals": {"margin": 13.13, "lean": 2.0, "environment": 8.3, "incumbency": 2.0, "money": 0.83}, "rating_margin": 13.9, "sigma_race": 5.5, "sigma_total": 6.37, "baseline_margin": 15.75, "analyst_adjustment": -0.25, "key_factors": ["Incumbent Goodlander holds a large polling lead, including a recent UNH survey showing a 21-point margin", "Strong fundraising edge with $2.7 million cash on hand versus under $700k for Tang Williams", "Expert ratings uniformly favor Democrats, ranging from Likely D to Safe D", "District's modest Democratic lean plus a favorable national environment"], "rationale": "Goodlander combines incumbency, a dominant money advantage, and consistent double-digit polling leads in a D+2 district, while every major rater places the race at Likely D or better and markets price her near certain. A rematch against Tang Williams, who lost here before, offers little evidence of movement toward Republicans.", "watch": "A late polling shift or heavy outside spending for Tang Williams could narrow the margin, though her limited resources make that unlikely.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Incumbent Maggie Goodlander (D) is running."]}, "overview": "Incumbent Democrat Maggie Goodlander faces a rematch with Republican Lily Tang Williams in New Hampshire's second district, a seat with a modest Democratic lean. Recent polling shows Goodlander well ahead, with the latest University of New Hampshire survey giving her a 21-point lead among likely voters, consistent with earlier Saint Anselm results in the mid-teens. She has also raised far more money, holding $2.7 million on hand to Williams' $628,000.\n\nEvery major race rater scores the contest as Likely D or better, and prediction markets put Goodlander's chances above ninety percent. The district's lean, her incumbency, and a favorable national environment all point the same direction. Williams ran a competitive race here in 2024, but nothing in the current evidence suggests a repeat of a close finish.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9818, "margin": 13.85}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9772, "margin": 13.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.978, "margin": 13.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9829, "margin": 15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9791, "margin": 15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.9795, "margin": 15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.9872, "margin": 15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.9799, "margin": 14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.9889, "margin": 15.5}]}